    "inputHash": "sha256:61d48e7ce3ba3467ac7e29d8e6a4840c3d1604397a8f5079e2f82889bab4e09c",
    "notes": "Stratford Railway Station includes the sweeping glazed Meridian Square hall, nine canopy families, the eastern lift, the open-top public footbridge and Meridian Steps. All four detail levels preserve five stair flights and four intermediate landings. Close-up represents 40 reconstructed treads. Platform grades, canopy supports and steps are visual reconstructions from standard terrain, mapped rail alignments and ordinary photographs. They have no surveyed rail clearances or accessibility data. The Westfield-side footbridge end is modeled to its mapped endpoint. The shopping centre, bus station, Stratford International and underground railway interiors use their own scene data."
  },
